unresolved.message:
@Josh Berman are these exposed by default now? 

Last I reviewed they were behind the little carrot on their own page

see mock here: https://www.figma.com/file/Tr5V91qdlhds6MhH1CCjp5/Cross-platform-suggest?type=design&node-id=1348%3A26704&mode=design&t=vnfIxNgd9iRFeWGo-1

@Misha Bruk @Jeff Pfaller 

Do we feel this warrants a new "section" or should the formatting read like a subsection of "Search" like the others (e.g. "Alternative Search Engines," Address bar - Firefox Suggest," etc.?

cc: @Josh Berman

First focusable element, <input type=search> with the label being the on-screen text "Search with Google or enter address".

@Misha Bruk I know It was not focusable with keyboard before to send users to type in their search in the awesomebar - would that still be the case?

Currently the search input is not focusable and (in the private window) is hidden from screen readers too. The latter would need not to happen for sure. And the former depends on the focus approach now :)

